Z||000000||yo_sweet||11-04-2001||10:14 AM||||my tranny is at the end of its life "i think"<BR>when i slam the gas to race the ricers it hits 80 km/h and then just revs up and down then ill have to slow down for it to kick in? any ideas? could it be the torque converter? my car has 112,xxx on it  i have a parts car that was well taken care of mechanicly it has 295,xxx on it should i swap trannies until i can afford to get mine rebult? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||California Kid||11-04-2001||10:26 AM||||Clutch plates are shot in the transmission or fluid valve body is varnished up (I would suspect the clutch plates first based on your miles). Do a full rebuild, don't trust old parts.||||reg||1
Z||000002||yo_sweet||11-04-2001||10:40 AM||||i will end up doing a rebuild but my fiero is a daily driver i was going to put the tranny in as a temporary replacemnt till i get the funds togeather , working at a golf coarse in canada dosen't help much eather!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-04-2001||12:19 PM||||Have the 295k tranny rebuilt while you're daily driver is still drivable.  Just take it easy.  You don't have to race everything that passes you.  I get challenged all the time, but I have 196k miles on my '86 and can't afford another motor right now so I just wave to them and wait for a curve.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Then I leave 'em in the dust.  Can't wait until I do the suspension.||||reg||1
Z||000004||p4n1c||11-04-2001||02:38 PM||||Mine was doing that in my Cutlass and it was a bearing in the clutch for third gear, metal shavings came off it and jammed in the pressure valves.  Is it also slipping?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mach10||11-04-2001||03:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by yo_sweet:<BR><B>my tranny is at the end of its life "i think"<BR>when i slam the gas to race the ricers it hits 80 km/h and then just revs up and down then ill have to slow down for it to kick in? any ideas? could it be the torque converter? my car has 112,xxx on it  i have a parts car that was well taken care of mechanicly it has 295,xxx on it should i swap trannies until i can afford to get mine rebult? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Assuming it's an auto (you never mentioned... Guessing from mention of Tq converter  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ), does it slip only while shifting, and catches? or does it ALWAYS slip in 3rd? If it only slips while shifting, then it's the brake bands. Needs a rebuild. If it always slips, then it's the clutch packs.<P>In either case, try giving it some new oil and a filter. Might help you out by shifting smoother, and not beating on the already half-dead parts.<P>With my Jag, you coul get away with extending the band-life by adjusting them... don't have a clue how to do this with a t-125<P>best bet is probably to rip one out of any 3-spd FWD 80s GM and transplant.<BR>||||reg||1
